 "_reference_comment": "REFERENCE section (#260, second pass). Each entry is what the reference decoder itself returns for that OGID: AnkiGammon's parse_ogid (ankigammon/utils/ogid.py, MIT, read at commit c5e71c3), run in Python on 2026-09-24 by a scratch script that dumped its Position.points (positive = White = P1, negative = Black = P2), its cube, dice, player on roll, points scored, match length and modifier. The strings are the examples of AnkiGammon's own README and tests/test_basic.py, plus positions chosen to cover what those do not: White on roll on an asymmetric board, checkers on both bars, the Crawford modifier and its absence at the same score, money play with an owned cube, a G modifier with a game count. The xgid of each entry is written from the reference's board by the same script (absolute board, field 5 Black's points, field 7 = 1 exactly when the modifier is C) — NOT by the reference's encode_xgid, which mirrors the board when White is on roll and so reads a different position than DecodeXGID does. pkg/blunderdb/domain/ogid_contract_test.go holds DecodeOGID to the decoded fields, to DecodeXGID, and EncodeOGID to a round trip.",
